{"tool_name":"validichro","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"validichro","home":"http://valispec.cryst.bbk.ac.uk/circularDichroism/ValiDichro/upload.html","license":"Unlicense","summary":"Web server for validating and quality control of protein circular dichromism spectra.","addition_date":"2017-03-25T16:29:53Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:04:45.688927Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:validichro","cost":"Free of charge","documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://valispec.cryst.bbk.ac.uk/circularDichroism/ValiDichro/uploadHelp.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Data handling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2409"},{"term":"Protein model validation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0321"},{"term":"Protein secondary structure assignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0319"},{"term":"Sequencing quality control","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3218"},{"term":"Validation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2428"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"ValiDichro","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkt287","metadata":{"abstract":"Circular dichroism (CD) spectroscopy is widely used in structural biology as a technique for examining the structure, folding and conformational changes of proteins. A new server, ValiDichro, has been developed for checking the quality and validity of CD spectral data and metadata, both as an aid to data collection and processing and as a validation procedure for spectra to be included in publications. ValiDichro currently includes 25 tests for data completeness, consistency and quality. For each test that is done, not only is a validation report produced, but the user is also provided with suggestions for correcting or improving the data. The ValiDichro server is freely available at http: